&lt;p&gt;Harbor &amp;amp; Pine runs the booking and payments platform behind 1,200 independent outdoor-gear rental shops across North America. Our Platform team owns the shared services every product team builds on: authentication, billing, event streaming and our internal developer portal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is an entry level position&lt;/strong&gt; on the Platform team, reporting to the Platform Engineering Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Design, build and operate highly available Go and TypeScript services on Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Own reliability for the services you build, including a 24/7 on-call rotation from your first month.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-team technical initiatives and mentor other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Drive architecture decisions for our Kafka-based event-streaming platform.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional software engineering experience required.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;3+ years operating Kubernetes in production.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with Kafka or a comparable streaming system.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading projects across multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;BS in Computer Science or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Terraform, AWS and Datadog.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments or marketplaces.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Remote (worldwide), with at least four hours of overlap with US Pacific time. Salary range for this Software Engineer I role: USD 95,000-115,000. Harbor &amp;amp; Pine is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
